_Balzers_-_Blick_auf_Gonzen.JPG/500px-Rhein_bei_Balzers_-_Blick_auf_Gonzen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Rhein_bei_Balzers_-_Blick_auf_Gonzen.JPG/1280px-Rhein_bei_Balzers_-_Blick_auf_Gonzen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Rhein_bei_Balzers_-_Blick_auf_Gonzen.JPG/500px-Rhein_bei_Balzers_-_Blick_auf_Gonzen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Rhine between Sargans in Switzerland (left) and Balzers in Liechtenstein (right) with the Gonzen (1,829 m (6,001 ft), left), the Girrenspitz (2,099 m (6,886 ft)) in the back, and the Maziferchopf (855 m (2,805 ft)) to the right","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARhein_bei_Balzers_-_Blick_auf_Gonzen.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Aerial_image_of_the_mouth_of_the_Rhine_into_Lake_Constance.jpg/500px-Aerial_image_of_the_mouth_of_the_Rhine_into_Lake_Constance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Aerial_image_of_the_mouth_of_the_Rhine_into_Lake_Constance.jpg/1280px-Aerial_image_of_the_mouth_of_the_Rhine_into_Lake_Constance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Aerial_image_of_the_mouth_of_the_Rhine_into_Lake_Constance.jpg/500px-Aerial_image_of_the_mouth_of_the_Rhine_into_Lake_Constance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aerial image of the mouth of the Rhine into Lake Constance","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAerial_image_of_the_mouth_of_the_Rhine_into_Lake_Constance.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Bodensee_satellit.jpg/500px-Bodensee_satellit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Bodensee_satellit.jpg/1280px-Bodensee_satellit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Bodensee_satellit.jpg/500px-Bodensee_satellit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Satellite image. In the center and on the right (i.e. to the east) the larger part of Lake Constance, called the Obersee, is visible, and it includes, in the lower right, the delta of the Alpine Rhine. The northwesterly \"finger\" (on the top left) is Lake Überlingen, containing the island of Mainau. Below Lake Überlingen (also in the west) is the smaller Untersee, containing Reichenau Island. The Obersee and Untersee are connected by the four kilometers long Seerhein. On the left the High Rhine can be seen.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABodensee_satellit.jpg"}],"sounds":{"rhine":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/61/En-us-Rhine.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/61/En-us-Rhine.ogg/En-us-Rhine.ogg.mp3"}],"river":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a5/En-uk-river.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a5/En-uk-river.ogg/En-uk-river.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e2/En-us-river.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e2/En-us-river.o